Package: arraydesignR
Title: Shiny App for Designing Acoustic Receiver Arrays
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Jacob", "Brownscombe", , "jakebrownscombe@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-2496-8764"))
Description: A Shiny application for designing acoustic receiver arrays and
    testing the performance of tracking systems on a depth raster, for a new
    study or to refine an array already in the water. Receivers are placed with
    'arraydesign', detection range is a depth-dependent logistic curve from
    'detfield', and the share of the water the array covers is computed with the
    distances through water, detection fields and array detection probability of
    'detfield', so the app and the packages give the same numbers for the same
    layout.
